description:
Proves the sixth case of Foulkes’ conjecture: \(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^bV)\) embeds equivariantly in \(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6V)\) for every <i>b</i> ≥ 6 and finite-dimensional complex <i>V</i>. More generally, the canonical multiplication map \(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^aV)	o\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^a(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^bV)\) is surjective for <i>a</i> ≥ 2 and \(b\ge a(a-1)\), giving dimension-independent quadratic stabilization. ([Lean](lean/docs/210.md))
